findings.body:
The PR is meant to remove a redundant `.clone()` in `WryWebviewDispatcher::delete_cookie`. The edit also changed the message variant from `WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie` to `WebviewMessage::SetCookie`. In the base, `set_cookie` (line 1705) already sends `SetCookie`, and `delete_cookie` correctly sent `DeleteCookie`. After this change both methods send `SetCookie`.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1711-1720"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The handler at lines 3737-3741 logs errors but never reports them back. Callers get `Ok(())` and no cookie is removed, so this will not surface as a crash or error.

The fix is to keep the `.into_owned()` cleanup and restore the variant:

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1718-1718"}
        WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie(cookie.into_owned()),

The rewritten `window_features` body has extra or missing spaces: `inner_size(size.width,    size.height)` and `position(position.x,position.y)`. The base had the standard form. `cargo fmt --check` will fail on these lines, which will break any formatting gate in CI.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1315-1322"}

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1317-1321"}
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.inner_size(size.width, size.height);
    }

    if let Some(position) = features.position() {
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.position(position.x, position.y);

`window_features` now applies `inner_size` before `position`. Nothing in the PR description mentions this. The tao-backed builder setters are independent, so the order does not change behavior. The reorder only adds noise to a diff that is already doing a rename.

Either drop the reorder or note in the PR why it was needed.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1315-1322"}

The created-window label in the API example changed from `new-{number}` to `new-window-{number}`. The PR description does not mention it, and it is not needed for the stated goals.

If the change is deliberate (for example, to avoid colliding with another label), say so in the PR. Otherwise revert it to keep the diff focused.

